# tests/lib's image (design/caos-expr.md, Phase 3): this directory is a flake
# (flake.nix + flake.lock + worker), so its image is the flake-builder applied
# to the directory itself — the same shape as every std entry. It names the
# builder by a LOCAL deep-deps mount, the only way anything here can name a
# builtin.
#
# It is under tests/ rather than std/ because it is test infrastructure, and it
# is an ENTRY rather than a harness because that is what lets a test ASK for it.
# dev/run-tests' fan-out skips directories with no `.caos-expr`; this one has
# one, so the skip is not what keeps it out of the suite — it has no `worker1`
# of its own to run, and nothing maps over it.
run --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/flake-builder --in:@=.
